.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pgdata/

# data/raw/*.csv.gz (the actual raw Kaggle data, gzipped) and
# data/export/*.gz (a pre-built ingest cache derived from it) are both
# deliberately TRACKED, not ignored — together they mean a fresh clone's
# `docker compose up` needs zero credentials and zero network calls beyond
# pulling Docker images: no Kaggle account, no manual data download. See
# DECISIONS.md's "Ingestion source" row for why. Only the plain, uncompressed
# .csv is ignored below — if you drop a fresh CSV from Kaggle directly into
# data/raw/ for local testing (DATA_SOURCE=raw reads it transparently either
# way, see ingest/ingest.py's open_raw()), it won't get accidentally committed
# uncompressed.
data/raw/*.csv

# Local-only full-embedding export (20,000 embedded rows), kept on this
# machine for convenience — too large (>100MB) to push to GitHub. The
# tracked data/export/news_headlines.copy.gz carries a smaller (10,000
# embedded row) subset instead so a fresh clone still gets working semantic
# search without hitting GitHub's file size limit.
data/export/*.local20k
